<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 12:38:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>南极血瀑布为何会喷出宝石红色的水？微生物提供了有关地质特征古代起源的新线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-does-antarcticas-blood-falls-spew-ruby-red-water-microbes-offer-new-clues-about-the-geologic-features-ancient-origins-180989271/</link><description>瀑布含有富含铁的盐水，当暴露在空气中时会氧化并变成红色。一项新的研究提供了进一步的证据，表明盐水可能来自数百万年前洪水退去时滞留的海水</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 20:26:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-does-antarcticas-blood-falls-spew-ruby-red-water-microbes-offer-new-clues-about-the-geologic-features-ancient-origins-180989271/</guid></item><item><title>在罗马斗兽场附近发现的这幅海洋生物马赛克提供了令人惊讶的线索——它的建筑可能是古罗马消防员的住所</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-marine-life-mosaic-discovered-near-the-colosseum-offers-a-surprising-clue-its-building-may-have-housed-firefighters-in-ancient-rome-180989273/</link><description>在公元二世纪建造这座建筑时，消防在古罗马已经是一个正式的职业</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:51:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-marine-life-mosaic-discovered-near-the-colosseum-offers-a-surprising-clue-its-building-may-have-housed-firefighters-in-ancient-rome-180989273/</guid></item><item><title>查尔斯·达尔文 (Charles Darwin) 推测这些植物在 150 年前是肉食性的。一项新研究证明他是对的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/charles-darwin-theorized-that-these-plants-were-carnivorous-150-years-ago-a-new-study-proves-him-right-180989265/</link><description>正如博物学家 1875 年预测的那样，一些虎耳草植物会捕食昆虫——利用粘性毛发来捕获昆虫</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:15:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/charles-darwin-theorized-that-these-plants-were-carnivorous-150-years-ago-a-new-study-proves-him-right-180989265/</guid></item><item><title>臭名昭著的野猫，以三年狩猎后捕获的稀有新西兰鸭子为食</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-lives-a-feral-cat-hunting-rare-ducks-in-new-zealand-has-been-caught-and-killed-after-three-years-180989267/</link><description>灰虎斑猫被称为“九命”，因为它多次逃脱捕获，它破坏了自然资源保护主义者将这种鸟类重新引入野外的努力</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 17:42:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-lives-a-feral-cat-hunting-rare-ducks-in-new-zealand-has-been-caught-and-killed-after-three-years-180989267/</guid></item><item><title>当金属探测器发现一条可追溯到青铜时代的金手镯时，他们认为自己中了大奖。然后他们又挖出了两个</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/metal-detectorists-thought-theyd-hit-the-jackpot-when-they-discovered-gold-bracelet-dating-to-bronze-age-then-they-found-two-more-180989272/</link><description>起初，安迪·克拉蒙德认为该物体是一个牛鼻环。附近出土的其他文物包括维京胸针、罗马钱币宝库和青铜时代斧头</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 17:39:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/metal-detectorists-thought-theyd-hit-the-jackpot-when-they-discovered-gold-bracelet-dating-to-bronze-age-then-they-found-two-more-180989272/</guid></item><item><title>火灾和财务问题使这座苏格兰城市的两家艺术机构的命运变得不确定——其中包括一件百年杰作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/fires-and-financial-trouble-leave-the-fate-of-a-few-arts-institutions-uncertain-in-this-scottish-city-including-a-century-old-art-nouveau-masterpiece-180989264/</link><description>历史悠久的格拉斯哥艺术学院和更现代的格拉斯哥当代艺术中心都受到了 2018 年重大火灾的影响</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 15:35:23 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/fires-and-financial-trouble-leave-the-fate-of-a-few-arts-institutions-uncertain-in-this-scottish-city-including-a-century-old-art-nouveau-masterpiece-180989264/</guid></item><item><title>当船只靠近时，抹香鲸似乎会改变叫声，凸显了水下噪音污染的影响</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/sperm-whales-seem-to-change-their-calls-when-ships-are-near-highlighting-the-implications-of-underwater-noise-pollution-180989257/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，生活在加勒比海东部的几种大型鲸类动物会缩短它们的点击间隔，并且当船只在附近时，它们会更多地使用一种点击模式。</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 15:12:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/sperm-whales-seem-to-change-their-calls-when-ships-are-near-highlighting-the-implications-of-underwater-noise-pollution-180989257/</guid></item><item><title>这艘因击沉敌舰而闻名的二战潜艇刚刚穿越密歇根湖进行了数百万美元的改造</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-world-war-ii-submaring-noted-for-its-success-sinking-enemy-ships-just-journeyed-across-lake-michigan-for-a-multimillion-dollar-makeover-180989269/</link><description>“银边”号航空母舰因其在太平洋的巡逻工作而赢得了十几颗战斗星。加托级潜艇现在是密歇根州博物馆的明星</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 14:48:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-world-war-ii-submaring-noted-for-its-success-sinking-enemy-ships-just-journeyed-across-lake-michigan-for-a-multimillion-dollar-makeover-180989269/</guid></item><item><title>AI 走进歌剧院，为瓦格纳首次上演这部杰作的剧院的《指环》周年纪念演出制作图像</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ai-went-to-the-opera-projecting-images-for-an-anniversary-production-of-wagners-ring-cycle-at-the-theater-where-he-first-staged-the-masterpiece-180989270/</link><description>理查德·瓦格纳花了四分之一个世纪才完成这部四部分歌剧。新作品名为“10010110”，利用生成人工智能来探索艺术品的演变</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 21:03:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ai-went-to-the-opera-projecting-images-for-an-anniversary-production-of-wagners-ring-cycle-at-the-theater-where-he-first-staged-the-masterpiece-180989270/</guid></item><item><title>海王星可能曾经见证过一场月球大屠杀，将其原来的卫星“翻了个底朝天”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/neptune-may-have-once-witnessed-a-lunar-massacre-that-turned-its-original-moons-inside-out-180989266/</link><description>一项新的研究在地球的两颗内卫星中发现了一种意想不到的矿物，指出了毁灭性的过去，其中一个大型物体被拉入该系统并摧毁了以前较大的卫星</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 20:51:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/neptune-may-have-once-witnessed-a-lunar-massacre-that-turned-its-original-moons-inside-out-180989266/</guid></item><item><title>受本杰明·富兰克林“加入或死亡”号召团结的启发，一座蛇形雕塑正在费城逐段成形</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-serpentine-sculpture-inspired-by-benjamin-franklins-join-or-die-call-for-unity-is-taking-shape-segment-by-segment-in-philadelphia-180989263/</link><description>这件 46 英尺长的花岗岩艺术品由约翰·柯林斯 (John Collins) 创作，灵感源自 18 世纪的政治漫画，预计将于今年秋天在独立广场 (Independence Mall) 揭幕</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 14:16:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-serpentine-sculpture-inspired-by-benjamin-franklins-join-or-die-call-for-unity-is-taking-shape-segment-by-segment-in-philadelphia-180989263/</guid></item><item><title>食肉“超级蠕虫”可能成为博物馆和研究标本的新骨骼清洁人员</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/flesh-eating-superworms-could-become-a-new-skeleton-cleaning-crew-for-museum-and-research-specimens-180989258/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，这些生物将是一种很好的替代方法，可以替代用于从骨头上去除肉的传统方法，包括皮甲虫、化学处理和煮沸，这些方法可能会造成损害或耗时</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/flesh-eating-superworms-could-become-a-new-skeleton-cleaning-crew-for-museum-and-research-specimens-180989258/</guid></item><item><title>这位美国飞行员在二战期间击落了 40 架敌机。研究人员在太平洋丛林中发现了他的飞机残骸，并将机翼带回了他的家乡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-american-pilot-downed-4o-enemy-aircraft-during-world-war-ii-researchers-discovered-the-wreck-of-his-plane-in-a-pacific-jungle-and-brought-a-wing-back-to-his-home-state-180989259/</link><description>理查德·奉邦 (Richard I. Bong) 驾驶着一架装饰着他未来妻子玛姬 (Marge) 肖像的飞机，成为美国得分最高的“王牌”，并获得了荣誉勋章</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 20:33:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-american-pilot-downed-4o-enemy-aircraft-during-world-war-ii-researchers-discovered-the-wreck-of-his-plane-in-a-pacific-jungle-and-brought-a-wing-back-to-his-home-state-180989259/</guid></item><item><title>两人感染环孢子虫病后死亡，这是与持续的多州疫情相关的首例已知死亡事件</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-peope-died-after-getting-sick-with-cyclosporiasis-marking-the-first-known-deaths-linked-to-the-ongoing-multi-state-outbreak-180989256/</link><description>据州官员称，这两名患者都在密歇根州，都有潜在的健康问题。寄生虫引起的感染通常不会危及生命</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 19:17:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-peope-died-after-getting-sick-with-cyclosporiasis-marking-the-first-known-deaths-linked-to-the-ongoing-multi-state-outbreak-180989256/</guid></item><item><title>多瑙河水位已降至历史最低水平，河道中的纳粹战舰、炸弹和猛犸象骨头都显露出来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-danube-river-has-fallen-to-record-low-water-levels-revealing-nazi-warships-bombs-and-woolly-mammoth-bones-in-its-channel-180989255/</link><description>随着欧洲第二长河流干涸，居民和研究人员正在寻找历史和史前遗迹</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 18:20:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-danube-river-has-fallen-to-record-low-water-levels-revealing-nazi-warships-bombs-and-woolly-mammoth-bones-in-its-channel-180989255/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家可能首次发现了一个徘徊到银河系边缘的超大质量黑洞</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-astronomers-may-have-spotted-a-supermassive-black-hole-that-wandered-to-the-edge-of-its-galaxy-180989233/</link><description>这些巨大的天体大部分是在星系中心被发现的，也就是它们所居住的地方。但最近发现的一个——由于它吞噬恒星时发出的光而被发现——似乎距离其宿主星系的中心超过 30,000 光年</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 16:16:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-astronomers-may-have-spotted-a-supermassive-black-hole-that-wandered-to-the-edge-of-its-galaxy-180989233/</guid></item><item><title>这些早期的双翼飞机记录了北极，拍摄了新闻短片并见证了林德伯格的历史性飞行。现在，一个罕见的例子将挂在博物馆里</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-early-biplanes-documented-the-arctic-captured-newsreel-footage-and-witnessed-lindberghs-historic-flight-now-a-rare-example-will-hang-in-a-museum-180989253/</link><description>航空摇篮博物馆最近购买了一架柯蒂斯金莺 (Curtiss Oriole)，这是在附近花园城工厂制造的三座双翼飞机</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 15:17:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-early-biplanes-documented-the-arctic-captured-newsreel-footage-and-witnessed-lindberghs-historic-flight-now-a-rare-example-will-hang-in-a-museum-180989253/</guid></item><item><title>古代北美哺乳动物可能在迁徙到南美洲之前聚集在墨西哥并实现多样化，从而促进它们在那里繁衍生息</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-north-american-mammals-may-have-gathered-in-mexico-and-diversified-before-moving-to-south-america-priming-them-to-thrive-there-180989251/</link><description>对来自该国的化石的分析表明，七百万至一千万年前，来自北方的动物生活在“围栏”中。这个时间线可能有助于解释为什么如此多的南美哺乳动物有北美血统，但反之则不然</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-north-american-mammals-may-have-gathered-in-mexico-and-diversified-before-moving-to-south-america-priming-them-to-thrive-there-180989251/</guid></item><item><title>为了找回被纳粹掠夺的艺术品，研究人员正在发挥创意，采取新策略，包括人工智能聊天机器人和“通缉”海报活动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/to-recover-artworks-looted-by-the-nazis-researchers-are-getting-creative-with-new-strategies-including-an-ai-chatbot-and-a-campaign-of-wanted-posters-180989247/</link><description>大学研究人员希望他们的新人工智能聊天机器人使来源研究变得更容易、更容易</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:33:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/to-recover-artworks-looted-by-the-nazis-researchers-are-getting-creative-with-new-strategies-including-an-ai-chatbot-and-a-campaign-of-wanted-posters-180989247/</guid></item><item><title>新图像提供了迄今为止最好的证据，证明超巨星参宿四确实有一个长期理论化的恒星伴星</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-images-provide-the-best-evidence-yet-that-supergiant-star-betelgeuse-does-inded-have-a-long-theorized-stellar-companion-180989225/</link><description>研究团队对这些数据基本信服，但他们希望在 2027 年捕获更多观察结果以证实他们的发现</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 20:07:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-images-provide-the-best-evidence-yet-that-supergiant-star-betelgeuse-does-inded-have-a-long-theorized-stellar-companion-180989225/</guid></item></channel></rss>